  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000124069,
      "SummaryText": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n- Accidental Release Prevention and Emergency Response Policies\n\nFlorida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, is strongly committed to employee, public, and environmental safety. This commitment is inherent to our comprehensive accidental release prevention program that covers areas such as design, installation, operating procedures, maintenance, and employee training associated with our regulated process. It is our policy to implement appropriate controls to prevent possible accidental releases of regulated substances. However, if such an accidental release does occur, we are coordinated with the Sumter County Fire Department and the Sumter County Local Emergency Planning Committee for emergency response support.\n\n- The Stationary Source and the Regulated Substances Handled\n\nPresently Anhydrous Ammonia is the only RMP regulated substance present at this facility above a threshold quantity.  Ammonia is utilized as the primary cooling media in our closed-loop refrigeration system. The system's purpose is to provide refrigeration and cold storage capabilities for Florida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, operations.  Due to the size and characteristics of our ammonia refrigeration systems, as well as Process Safety Management (PSM) applicability, Florida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, is covered under Program 3 of the RMP regulations.\n\n- General Accidental Release Prevention Program \n\nFlorida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, has taken all necessary steps to comply with the accidental release prevention requirements set forth in 40 CFR Part 68.  To meet these necessary requirements Florida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, has implemented their Process Safety Management program through the written guidelines stated in the OSHA PSM Standard, 29 CFR 1910.119. \n\n- Accident History\n\nIn the past five years, Florida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, has not experienced any accidental releases of ammonia that resulted in on site or off site impacts, or that required reporting.  \n \n\n- E"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000124069,
      "SummaryText": "mergency Action/Response Plan\n\nFlorida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL is included in the written community emergency response plan.  The facility has its own emergency action plan.  The emergency action plan includes procedures for informing the public and local response agencies of a chemical release.  The emergency action plan also includes information on emergency health care.\n\nFlorida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL does not respond to emergencies.  Fresh Express coordinates its Emergency Action Plan with the Sumter County Fire Rescue. \n\n- Planned Changes to Improve Safety:\n\nFlorida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, currently has no changes planned for the ammonia refrigeration processes at this time.   However, the processes will be subjected to periodic process hazard analysis reviews for the purpose of identifying potential hazards and implementing the necessary improvement to provide a safer system. Florida Beef, Inc., Center Hill, FL, personnel will also periodically review all potential opportunities to improve the safety of our personnel, the surrounding community, and the ammonia refrigeration processes."
    }
